- `git diff --check`: `0`.
- Full `swift test`: `1`; all 455 tests ran, with the existing 25 known unavailable-adapter issues plus one unrelated libssh2 `clientAndServerRekey` close-state timing failure. Exact `mandatoryGate` rerun: `0`, all 18 rows passed with nine known unavailable-adapter issues. Logs: `.temp/TASK-260715-1idq8c/swift-test-02.log` and `.temp/TASK-260715-1idq8c/swift-test-mandatory-gate-04.log`. The anomaly is recorded in `LOGBOOK.md`; UI-specific suites pass through `make apple-ui-test-contract` and the iOS XCUITest smoke.

## Mandatory visual review

Both final iOS Simulator screenshots in `run.Xcqjbb` were opened at original resolution:

- `Step_01__diagnostic_fixture_ready_*.png`: portrait orientation; centered, unclipped layout; expected diagnostic, safety-boundary, action, and awaiting-confirmation content readable; non-black/non-empty rendering.
- `Step_02__diagnostic_fixture_confirmed_*.png`: portrait orientation; centered, unclipped layout; expected diagnostic, safety-boundary, action, and confirmed content readable; non-black/non-empty rendering.

The controlled `diff.png` was also opened and visibly highlights the deliberate mismatch.

## Safety, privacy, and residual risks

No signing, notarization, native macOS app/test launch, product/provider installation or launch, NetworkExtension approval, VPN preference create/save/enable/start, route, DNS, interface, or packet-filter mutation occurred. The iOS runtime used only the isolated Simulator fixture. Device identifiers and signing material are omitted from this outcome.

Native signed macOS fixture-host/XCUITest runtime proof remains owned by `TASK-260822-3q4grm` on the dedicated test Mac; this is an accepted evidence split, not a hidden build-host pass. Physical-device rows remain separate future evidence. Product-screen snapshot baselines are intentionally absent until product screens exist; the current task proves the deterministic failure-artifact workflow without inventing business UI.
